# Two trees on different but overlapping taxon sets: neither contains all of
# a, b, c, d, e. Their clusters are *partial* -- a tree says nothing about the
# taxa it is missing -- so plain Cass refuses this input.
#
#   phylocass examples/partial_trees.newick               refuses, and says why
#   phylocass examples/partial_trees.newick --z-closure   completes and builds
#
# Z-closure extends {a,b} and {a,c} to the full taxon set and derives {a,b,c},
# leaving a genuine conflict that needs one reticulation.
(((a,b),c),d);
(((a,c),b),e);
